{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicHierarchy"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.sdp_degenerate_locus_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.sdp_degenerate_locus_two","kind":"theorem","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L445-L460","doc":"**The n=2 case is now DERIVED, not assumed** — and this is what the\nencoding buys beyond legibility.\n\n§3b-cond item 5 forbids a class that carries its own conclusion as a field\nwith a \"theorem\" that projects it.  Here the class carries the *bridge*\n(`degenerate_two`) and this theorem composes it with\n`silver_lp_coincidence`, which is proved sorry-free above.  So the class\nsupplies a hypothesis and Lean supplies the mathematics — the honest shape.\n\nNote what is NOT used: the `holds` field.  The `n = 2` locus follows from\nthe bridge alone, which says the general conjecture is doing no work at\n`n = 2` and is exactly as strong as its `n ≥ 3` content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.holds","kind":"theorem","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L438-L438","doc":"**The conjecture**: every degenerate locus is a metallic ratio —\n`S(n) ⊆ {δ_1, …, δ_n}`.\n\nWas `holds : Prop`, so an instance chose it and `⟨True⟩` discharged the\nwhole class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.degenerate_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.degenerate_two","kind":"theorem","line":432,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L432-L432","doc":"**The bridge hypothesis**: at `n = 2`, degeneracy IS cost coincidence.\nThis is the assumption that connects the SDP notion above to the LP\nidentities this file proves sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.IsDegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.IsDegenerate","kind":"def","line":428,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L428-L428","doc":"`IsDegenerate n q` — the n-strand LP's optimal face has positive\ndimension at `q` (strict complementarity fails).  Carried as a field\nbecause the parametric-SDP machinery that would define it is not in the\nframework; that absence is what makes this class conditional, and saying\nso in the type is the point of the encoding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L422-L422","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.SDPDegeneracyDetectsMetallic","kind":"class","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L417-L439","doc":"Conjectural witness: cost-coincidence points are EXACTLY the loci of\nSDP degeneracy (strict-complementarity failure) on the metallic\nladder.  Discharging requires the parametric-SDP machinery: the\noptimal-face dimension as a function of q has discontinuities at\nmetallic ratios. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.n2_lp_degenerate_at_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.n2_lp_degenerate_at_silver","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L402-L415","doc":"Helper: the n=2 LP is degenerate at q = δ_silver.\n\nStated as: any feasible x with `x_1 + x_2 = n_target` achieves the\nsame cost.  In SDP language, the optimal face has dimension ≥ 1\ninstead of being a vertex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition.holds","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L380-L380","doc":"**The conjecture**: the boundary lies at `q = φ²`, the bar image of\n`q_gold = 1/φ²`.  `φ` is `metallic 1`.\n\nWas `holds : Prop`.  Falsifiable via a second kink in the neutron-star\nmass-radius relation above the silver-density crossover — a falsifiable\nclaim that the `Prop` field could not state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition.q_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition.q_boundary","kind":"def","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L373-L373","doc":"The CFL → gCFL (or CCS) phase boundary, as a value of the substrate\nmodulus `q`.  A field because the framework does not derive it; the\nconjecture is about where it sits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L369-L369","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.BarMirrorPhi2CFLgCFLTransition","kind":"class","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L364-L380","doc":"Conjectural witness: the bar-image φ² of the deconfinement boundary\n`q_gold = 1/φ²` predicts a CFL → gCFL (gapless CFL) or CCS\n(crystalline color superconductor) phase boundary at q = φ² ≈ 2.618.\nFalsifiable via a second kink in the neutron-star mass-radius\nrelation above the silver-density crossover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.holds","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L360-L360","doc":"**The conjecture**: the cost-coincidence locus `q = δ_silver` of the n=2\nLP maps to the CFL transition density.\n\nWas `holds : Prop`, so the instance chose what \"equals\" meant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.rho_c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.rho_c","kind":"def","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L355-L355","doc":"The CFL transition density `ρ_c` predicted by\nconj:color-superconductivity-borromean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.rho","kind":"def","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L352-L352","doc":"The substrate-density correspondence `q ↦ ρ`.  The class docstring says\nthis map is \"not yet pinned in the framework\"; carrying it as a field is\nhow that shows up in the type instead of only in prose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L348-L348","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.CSCSilverIsCFLTransition","kind":"class","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L344-L360","doc":"Conjectural witness: the n=2 LP active-set transition at δ_silver\nphysically identifies the Color-Flavor-Locked transition density ρ_c.\nConditional on the q-ρ map (substrate-density correspondence not\nyet pinned in the framework). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.holds","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L339-L339","doc":"**The conjecture**: for every `q > 0` and every partition `λ`,\n`χ^λ(σ_i) + χ^{λ'}(σ_i) = dim(λ) · (q − q⁻¹)`.\n\nEmpirically verified for partitions of `n ∈ {3, 4}`; a direct\nconsequence of `A_λ + A_{λ'} = dim λ`, from SYT right-of / below counts\nbeing swapped under transpose.\n\nWas `holds : Prop` — a field typed with the UNIVERSE `Prop`, so the\ninstance supplied the proposition and `⟨True⟩` inhabited the class.\nEncoded 2026-09-07 per §3b-tax: an unproved primary is a content-bearing\nclass with no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.dim","kind":"def","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L327-L327","doc":"Wedderburn dimension `dim λ` (the SYT count). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.conj","kind":"def","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L325-L325","doc":"Conjugate partition `λ ↦ λ'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.chi","kind":"def","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L323-L323","doc":"The Hecke character `χ^λ` evaluated at a braid generator, as a function\nof `q`.  Carried as a field rather than referenced: the Hoefsmit-Wenzl\ncharacter machinery is not in this framework, and that absence is\nexactly what makes this class conditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L318-L318","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.GaloisPairCharacterSum","kind":"class","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L314-L340","doc":"Conjectural witness for the Galois-pair character sum identity.\nSymbolically verified for partitions of n=3, n=4 in\n`metallic_q_symbolic_galois_proofs.py`.  Lean discharge requires\nSYT counting + Hoefsmit-Wenzl character machinery from Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.hecke_scalar_integer_iff_metallic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.hecke_scalar_integer_iff_metallic","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L301-L310","doc":"The Hecke scalar `q − q⁻¹` takes an integer value (n ≥ 0) at q > 0\nif and only if q is a metallic ratio `δ_n`.  This is the algebraic\nexplanation for why the Mahler-height proxy drops sharply at metallic\nratios — the value `q − q⁻¹` becomes a small integer with height\n`log(n + 1)`.  Discharged by `MetallicHierarchy.metallic_iff_hecke_scalar`\n(PR #1999); the metallic ratio `δ_n` is `QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.phi_squared_between_silver_and_bronze","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.phi_squared_between_silver_and_bronze","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L254-L297","doc":"φ² ≈ 2.618; silver ≈ 2.414; bronze ≈ 3.303.  So φ² is between silver\nand bronze, predicting a sub-CFL phase transition there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.q_gold_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.q_gold_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L240-L252","doc":"`q_gold = (3 − √5)/2`, the explicit numerical form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.q_gold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.q_gold","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L237-L238","doc":"The deconfinement boundary `q_gold = 1/φ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.phi_squared_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.phi_squared_eq","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L230-L235","doc":"`φ² = φ + 1 = (3 + √5)/2`.  Follows from `φ² − φ − 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.phi","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L227-L228","doc":"The golden ratio `φ = (1 + √5)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.cost_coincidence_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.cost_coincidence_unique","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L210-L218","doc":"The cost-coincidence is unique on q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.silver_lp_coincidence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.silver_lp_coincidence","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L178-L208","doc":"**Main theorem**: the n=2 LP cost-coincidence `t_1(q) = t_2(q)` holds\nif and only if `q = δ_silver`.  This pins the empirical \"S(2) = {silver}\"\nfinding from the LP active-set sweep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.cost_coincidence_iff_hecke_scalar_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.cost_coincidence_iff_hecke_scalar_two","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L155-L176","doc":"The cost-coincidence equation `t_1(q) = t_2(q)` over `q > 0` reduces\nto `q − q⁻¹ = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.t2_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.t2_n2","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L152-L153","doc":"`t_2(q) = q² − q⁻²`, the Markov trace of σ_0 at strand count 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.t1_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.t1_n2","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L149-L150","doc":"`t_1(q) = 2(q + q⁻¹)`, the Markov trace of γ at strand count 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_inv_eq_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_inv_eq_bar","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L140-L145","doc":"The bar involution image of `δ_silver`: explicit form `√2 − 1 ≈ 0.414`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_eq_metallic_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_eq_metallic_two","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L115-L138","doc":"`δ_silver` is the `n = 2` rung of the metallic hierarchy\n(`QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic`): both are the unique positive root\nof `x² − 2x − 1`.  Bridge lemma for unifying downstream local\ndefinitions (e.g. `MetallicSilverFamily.deltaSilver`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_hecke_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_hecke_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L109-L113","doc":"`δ_silver − δ_silver⁻¹ = 2`, the integer Hecke-scalar value at silver. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_inv","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L101-L107","doc":"`δ_silver⁻¹ = δ_silver − 2 = √2 − 1`.  This IS the bar image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L94-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_pos","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L89-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_satisfies_minpoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver_satisfies_minpoly","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L80-L87","doc":"`δ_silver` satisfies the integer-coefficient minimal polynomial\n`x² − 2x − 1 = 0`.  Pisot signature: integer-monic quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicLPIdentities.delta_silver","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicLPIdentities.lean#L77-L78","doc":"The silver metallic ratio `δ_2 = 1 + √2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}